{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Store only the SET of Jira keys seen last pass instead of the full ACLI payload. prev_snapshot is\n**228.1 MB / 4.5 MB per day** — the largest term after A1. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Measured effect\nOver the newest **400 real revisions**: **218 of 399** consecutive pairs have an **identical key\nset** (so they become byte-identical and produce no commit at all), and when it changes the mean\nsymmetric difference is **1.78 keys**. Key-set payload at HEAD is **19,960 bytes** vs a **27.1 MB**\nfull payload.\n\n## Why this is safe — gate G1 was cleared empirically, not by reasoning\nA corpus mutation-diff ran the real differ plus the production\n`drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` call-site filter over **four real snapshot pairs**\nwith full prev vs key-set prev and found **zero difference in any observable mutation effect**.\nThat filter is the load-bearing production guarantee: `run_differs.py` applies it before dispatch\nand drops both `(outbound, create, unbound_local)` and `(outbound, update, field_drift)` for either\nprev shape. Its removal note remains coupled to a future migration that passes real local state.\nBranch-3 also has defense in depth: `_mutation_to_batch_dict` reads\n`payload[\"changed_fields\"]` for updates, which branch-3 never sets, so `fields` collapses to `{}`\nand `update_issue(key)` short-circuits with zero subprocess and zero network.\n\n**It also removes wasted raw mutations.** With a full prev, keys in prev-but-not-curr make\n`compute_mutations` emit 973-998 `(outbound, create, unbound_local)` mutations when the fetch\nwindow shrinks or the project is re-targeted. The existing call-site filter already prevents\nthose raw emissions from reaching `create_one` at HEAD. A key-set eliminates them at the source,\nreducing differ work and mutation-cap pressure without claiming a new Jira-facing behavior change.\n\nShape constraint: store a **dict** `{jira_key: {}}`, not a `set`. The prev-shape-sensitive\nconsumers exercised here are `check_dual_identity_complete` and the differ's local-only / emit-both\narms, whose `local_state[key] or {}` guards require mapping entries. The binding walk consumes\n`curr_snapshot` and a mutation-derived adopt-skip set, so it is unaffected. On the first pass after\ncutover the new reader tolerates an old full-payload prev; the same pass writes the key-set shape,\nand the committed full-vs-key-set corpus plus invariant tests cover that coexistence.\n\n## Rollback (mandatory artifact)\nThe committed corpus runs both forward (full -> key-set) and backward (key-set -> full, the revert\ndirection) comparisons. Deleting `prev_snapshot.json` is **not** a safe default escape hatch: an\nempty prev makes the differ re-derive inbound creates for curr-only keys unless a `rebar-id:` label\nsuppresses them. If deletion is ever used, it MUST be followed by a cap-0/no-write pass proving\nzero unexpected inbound creates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Corpus mutation-diff (full prev vs key-set prev) over **>=4 real snapshot pairs** shows **zero\n      difference** in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect. Tier: **repo-level corpus\n      script** committed under the experiments path.\n- [x] The **reverse-direction** diff (key-set -> full) is recorded on this ticket as the rollback\n      artifact, showing the revert path emits no unexpected inbound creates. Tier: **repo-level\n      corpus script**.\n- [x] Branch-2 regression is gone: with a key-set prev and >=900 prev-only keys, **zero**\n      `(outbound, create)` mutations are emitted. Tier: **unit** on `compute_mutations`.\n- [x] `check_dual_identity_complete` behaves identically for full-payload and `{}` prev entries.\n      Tier: **unit**.\n- [x] The differ's local-only and emit-both arms preserve their intended outcomes with `{}` prev\n      entries, including no field-bearing mutation reaching Jira unexpectedly. Tier: **unit**.\n- [x] prev_snapshot at HEAD is <=64 KB after one pass. Verify: byte measurement.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` (prev persist),\n`run_differs.py`, `differ.py`, tests, corpus script\n\nScope: M. Depends on A4-1."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785724670784527001,"uuid":"8effa947-fa14-4ca8-9f18-bfd9f827af35"}